 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Text: Who will collect the rubbish?\nIn our town, the council's trucks collect refuse from large bins along the main roads. But many quarters have no bins, so people throw their rubbish into gutters, rivers or empty plots. When it rains, the blocked gutters overflow and flood the houses. Some people burn their rubbish, and the smoke makes children cough. The trucks are too few and they sometimes do not come for a week. Last month, the youths of our quarter organised a clean-up campaign. They cleared the gutters, put up signs saying \"No dumping\", and asked the council to place a bin at the junction. Now every family carries its rubbish there in a closed bag.\n\nWords: refuse (rubbish, garbage), a bin, a dump, to dispose of, a gutter, to overflow, a clean-up campaign, biodegradable, recycling.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "What problems does rubbish cause in the text?",
  "steps": [
   "Find what happens when people throw rubbish anywhere or burn it.",
   "Blocked gutters overflow and flood houses; smoke makes children cough."
  ],
  "answer": "floods from blocked gutters; smoke that makes children cough",
  "checks": []
 },
